---
layout: layout.njk
title: Build
description: "How the work gets built: one founder, a team of AI agents, and every decision written down."
permalink: /build/index.html
---
<section class="page-intro accent-ticket">
  <p class="eyebrow">Build / How we work</p><h1>One founder. A team of agents. Everything written down.</h1><p class="lede">We build in the open about how, and carefully about what. One person decides; a team of AI agents, each with one job, specifies, builds, reviews and tests.</p><p class="status">Work in progress</p>
</section>
<section class="numbers-strip" aria-label="By the numbers">
  <p class="eyebrow">By the numbers</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>{{ numbers.updates }}</strong><span>updates installed since {{ numbers.updatesSince }}</span></li>
    <li><strong>{{ numbers.changes }}</strong><span>changes in those updates since {{ numbers.changesSince }}</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p class="strip-note">Counted by script on {{ numbers.countedOn }}: installed updates, and the pull requests merged into them.</p>
</section>
<section class="editorial section">
  <h2>How decisions get made</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>The founder decides what gets built. Each decision is recorded in her own words, so there is always a plain answer to “why is it like this?”</p><p>Nothing ships on a summary. Money, access and tax work gets a security review before it merges, and the founder installs each build herself, with a way back ready.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="evidence-panel" aria-labelledby="status-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Where things stand</p><h2 id="status-title">What it does on a shift, in three lists.</h2>
  <h3 class="built-heading">Built</h3>
  <ul class="built-list">
    {% for b in built %}
    <li class="built-item{% if not b.images.length %} no-shot{% endif %}">
      <p>{{ b.text }}</p>
      {% if b.images.length %}<div class="built-figs">{% for img in b.images %}<figure class="built-fig"><a href="{{ img.light }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img class="built-shot theme-light" src="{{ img.light }}" alt="{{ img.alt }}" loading="lazy"></a><a href="{{ img.dark }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img class="built-shot theme-dark" src="{{ img.dark }}" alt="{{ img.alt }}" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>The app today</figcaption></figure>{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <div class="evidence-grid">
    <div>
      <h3>In the works</h3>
      <ul class="status-list">
        <li>Custom roles that take orders on the register.</li>
        <li>Staff sales that follow a check when it’s handed to someone else.</li>
        <li>“My checks”: each person’s own checks, handed over cleanly when a shift changes.</li>
        <li>Seats shown on the kitchen screen.</li>
        <li>A notification center.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Coming</h3>
      <ul class="status-list">
        <li>Approvals from a manager’s phone.</li>
        <li>Kitchen alerts when food is ready.</li>
        <li>Sizes and price levels.</li>
        <li>More discount options.</li>
        <li>Report screens, and ticket print options.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="status">Not scheduled yet: card payments, and a live view of the tip pool so everyone in it sees their share.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="editorial section" aria-labelledby="latest-title">
  <h2 id="latest-title">Latest update</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    {% set latest = updates | first %}
    <h3>{{ latest.name }}</h3>
    <p>{{ latest.intro }}</p>
    <ul>
      {% for item in latest.items %}<li>{{ item }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="status">Older updates</p>
    {% for u in updates %}{% if not loop.first %}
    <details class="update-fold">
      <summary>{{ u.name }}</summary>
      <p>{{ u.intro }}</p>
      <ul>
        {% for item in u.items %}<li>{{ item }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </details>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
<section class="editorial section" aria-labelledby="unproven-title">
  <h2 id="unproven-title">Not proven yet</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>This is an experiment, not something to run a live restaurant on yet. Three things we have not proven:</p>
    <ul class="status-list">
      <li>That the floor keeps working through a real internet outage. It is built to; we haven't shown it end to end.</li>
      <li>That several people can change the same check on a busy night without anything going wrong.</li>
      <li>That it recovers cleanly after a failure, and works with every printer and card reader a restaurant might use.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="invitation compact">
  <h2>Have a question about how it’s built?</h2><p>Write to us.</p><a class="button" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email {{ site.email }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</section>
